    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The search giant that pioneered new digital territories is now caged by its own design. European authorities are closing in on a massive antitrust fine for demoting explorers of comparison to favor its own mapped territories, actions violating EU competition law. This financial penalty, set to be finalized before the Commission's recess, underscores the challenge of navigating the frontier of digital regulation.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Explorer",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "why-1",
          "how-2",
          "how-3",
          "result-0"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.78
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "For more than two years, regulators in the EU have led an investigation into a tech platform caging rivals. Now, a formal decision on a large financial penalty is imminent, a moment for the walled jurisdiction to mark a new boundary. This monetary sanction, another in a long series of accumulated competition fines, will be a significant test of the new frontier rules designed to open closed ecosystems.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Explorer",
